                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "205e8e56-b447-3d08-802f-71a4955450d5",
                        "entry_id": "aa1a98a5-f044-39e1-b8cd-2a6668fdae2f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. поведение, образ жизни дармоеда; проживание на чужие средства, тунеядство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8204cd14-6ed6-4012-a723-cf34868d7261",
                                "sense_id": "205e8e56-b447-3d08-802f-71a4955450d5",
                                "text": "Пчёлкин не обладал достаточной физической силой и, как человек вполне городской, не привык к физическому труду, так что от него хозяйкам было мало пользы, однако он никогда не отказывался от работы, даже сам напрашивался на неё, чувствуя неловкость за своё дармоедство, и рад был поковыряться вилами в сухих табачных пластах старого навоза или перетащить на спине в плетёную клуню два-три не слишком тяжёлых мешка с отрубями или кукурузными початками."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e210f6cf-29e3-4a78-9578-f01561c6eeeb",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa1a98a5-f044-39e1-b8cd-2a6668fdae2f",
                        "source_sense_id": "205e8e56-b447-3d08-802f-71a4955450d5",
                        "target_lang_word": "parasitism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parasitism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d3399f7-f4e5-3a1e-8f9c-e01e342b37a8",
                                        "entry_id": "c66933b9-950f-333d-b988-bd3d123182e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Interaction between two organisms, in which one organism (the parasite) benefits and the other (the host) is harmed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28cecb6b-62db-3b88-b61e-976d7a194f8d",
                                        "entry_id": "c66933b9-950f-333d-b988-bd3d123182e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A similar interaction between people or things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "814a3fcf-8266-4d32-bf8c-138002111241",
                                                "sense_id": "28cecb6b-62db-3b88-b61e-976d7a194f8d",
                                                "text": "We accused her of parasitism in taking his hard-earned money for new dresses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad1d6cb8-9d5b-422d-9ce0-9a9abfb85c2d",
                                                "sense_id": "28cecb6b-62db-3b88-b61e-976d7a194f8d",
                                                "text": "These devices' energy consumption is parasitism upon the electrical grid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb682773-8c43-4e56-b481-d305c6b63a44",
                                                "sense_id": "28cecb6b-62db-3b88-b61e-976d7a194f8d",
                                                "text": "Either theſe men imagine themſelves to be marvelouſly high ſet and exalted in the chair of Belfaſt, to vouchſafe the parliament of England no better ſtile than Servants, or elſe their high notion, which we rather believe, falls as low as court paraſitiſm ; ſuppoſing all men to be ſervants, but the king."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d7ca698-d98d-4668-b2c5-9b5aec02b361",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa1a98a5-f044-39e1-b8cd-2a6668fdae2f",
                        "source_sense_id": "205e8e56-b447-3d08-802f-71a4955450d5",
                        "target_lang_word": "sponging",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sponging",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc42de9e-33a8-3a32-8b65-febac2c61f78",
                                        "entry_id": "006c3d50-b721-3650-accc-dcc9e6b3bc13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of sponge"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e70fea6-cf59-49f2-80fe-a73f0fec2756",
                                                "sense_id": "bc42de9e-33a8-3a32-8b65-febac2c61f78",
                                                "text": "I'm to be a poor, crawling beggar, sponging for rum, when I might be rolling in a coach!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sponging",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7f7cfaf-85e3-3d09-8906-4c8c8e1ab99b",
                                        "entry_id": "38b77da0-5c43-3eeb-a25c-f47baa6c3a63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The application of a sponge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c62048b-fcbb-472d-96f3-c57dd5042154",
                                                "sense_id": "c7f7cfaf-85e3-3d09-8906-4c8c8e1ab99b",
                                                "text": "I have employed cold air, and very often spongings with cold water, in order to moderate the preternatural heat of the skin, and to check the increased velocity of the circulation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
